# Astro extracts a page's script and style blocks into _astro/, and GitHub Pages runs Jekyll by
# default — which silently drops every directory whose name starts with an underscore. The result is
# a site whose markup is there and whose module scripts all 404, so nothing that needs JavaScript
# ever upgrades (a page whose only styling lives in public/styles/ looks fine, which is what made
# this hard to see). This file turns that off. Keep it: without it the deploy is a static facade.
